<title>USA: FP&amp;L St Lucie 1 Fla. nuclear unit restarts.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L St Lucie 1 Fla. nuclear unit restarts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power and Light Co's 839 megawatt (MW) St Lucie 1 nuclear unit was operating at 10 percent power early Friday morning, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said in its plant status report.  </p>
<p>The unit, in Hutchinson Island, Fla., tripped off line Tuesday afternoon due to a faulty circuit breaker, the company reported earlier this week.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with an identical generating capacity, was operating at full power, the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>FP&amp;L is a subsidiary of FPL Group Inc.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
